  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **There is Power in a Union** (1 other source): This song is a cover of a Billy Bragg song [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Idylls of the King**: rare: 11 archived performances [3]\n- **Doc Gooden**: rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n- **Hebrews 11:40**: back after 43 archived shows (378 days); rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n- **There is Power in a Union**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2024-08-15.wav** (recommended): source not stated; 22 songs; 102 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The band walked on to Bob Marley & The Wailers' \"Three Little Birds\" as intro music [1]\n- The reviewer ranks this among their favorite tours and enjoyed hearing how the songs developed in the trio format [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2024-08-15.wav**: taped by SkeletonCounter; source: Zoom H2n [1]. Also: Recorded with a light, affordable rig built around an h2(n) recorder, which the listener says performs far above its price [2]",
